"[HEADER] Installation Infos",
"kill",
"When you click 'START SETUP' in the 'SETUP' tab, fnafw.apworld will be installed and moved into the 'custom_worlds' folder inside the Archipelago Launcher directory. A copy of the game's .exe file (fnaf-world.exe) will be created inside a new 'FNaFW Game' folder in the Archipelago directory. You don't need to have the game already installed on your PC, the tool will download it for you.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] apworld / yaml Infos",
"kill",
"FNaF World is not a core Archipelago game, it needs a custom world file. When 'fnafw.apworld' is downloaded in the Archipelago Folder (by clicking START SETUP), boot-up the Archipelago Launcher and go to 'Options Creator' to create your .yaml file and then, when you're done, send it to the person who will host the AP Multiworld.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Connection Infos",
"kill",
"Once you have used the setup, a new 'FNaF World Client' will be created inside the Archipelago Launcher, open this client from the Launcher.\n\nOn the client, in the bottom input field, type '/patch'. Once the command is done, a new patched version version of the game's executable file will be created next to the one that was just copied by the setup (should be at: 'C:\\ProgramData\\Archipelago\\FNaFW Game\\FNaFW Modded.exe').\n\nOn the client again, in the top input field this time, type your multiworld's server address and press 'Connect' (see the 'HOSTING' tab if you want infos about generating a multiworld). When it asks you to enter your slot name, type the name attached to your YAML file. Finally, simply open the patched version of the game and it should connect you and give you your starting character (FNaFW Modded.exe).",
"kill",
"[HEADER] Revert Infos",
"kill",
"Reverting will delete the 'FNaFW Game' folder from the Archipelago directory.",
"kill",
"[HEADER] PopTracker Infos",
"kill",
"Some games have a PopTracker integration for Archipelago which allows you to track all possible Locations, Items, Upgrades, Zones, Hints and more depending on the game.\n\nFor the setup there are 3 different cases:\n\n\t• If the selected directory does not contain a PopTracker folder (or any similarly named folder), a new 'poptracker' folder will be created and the pack will be downloaded to poptracker\\packs.\n\n\t• If the selected directory already contains a folder with 'PopTracker' in its name, the installer will look for a poptracker.exe file. If one is found, the pack will be downloaded to its packs folder. If no poptracker.exe is found, the folder will be renamed to 'poptracker' and any missing files or folders will be created.\n\n\t• If the selected directory is already a PopTracker folder (for example: C:\\Users\\magni\\Documents\\poptracker), its contents will be validated. If everything is present, the pack will simply be downloaded to poptracker\\packs. Otherwise, the folder will be repaired before the pack is installed.",
"clear"

